 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No shirt, face or eyes drawn; light for «فارتد بصيرا». Their «إنك لفي ضلالك القديم» (95) is framed by As-Sa'di's «فوقع ما ظنه بهم» (the mockery Ya'qub foresaw). Geometric for «أعلم من الله ما لا تعلمون» and «إنه هو الغفور الرحيم», a door for «ادخلوا مصر» (it leaves before «إن شاء الله»). 94:4-9 is not glossed. STAGING v4: At Ya'qub's tents in the desert (12:100). Ya'qub is only a blue drop labelled Ya'qub; Yusuf is not on stage in this video. c1 (94-95): a footsteps plate as the caravan sets out from Egypt (94:2-6); Ya'qub speaks to those with him (94:4, 94:10), a plain group of three (Al-Muyassar: those present; As-Sa'di 96: his children and family who were with him); they answer him (95:1) and their words are framed by the gloss. c2 (96): the bearer of good news, a single traveller (the tafsirs do not name him), comes in and walks to Ya'qub (96:3); no shirt, face or eyes are drawn, and no light, glow or sparkle marks the return of his sight (96:5-9); Ya'qub speaks to those present (96:10, 96:14), with a geometric plate for I know from Allah (96:15-17). c3 (97-99): his sons (a plain group of three (3 figures = a group, not their number)) ask him to seek forgiveness (97:1, 97:6; no bowing toward the drop) and he answers (98:1) with a geometric plate for He is the Forgiving, the Merciful (98:6). 99: the family sets out for Egypt from the camp (Al-Muyassar: Ya'qub and his family went out to Egypt seeking Yusuf): Ya'qub's drop moves to his sons (99:1), they turn (99:2) and all leave by the left (exit 99:4). The meeting itself is not staged: from 99:5 to the end the camera stays wide on the empty camp (one wide shot at 99:6 only for the 6 s density rule, no actor beat on 99:5-7); nothing is drawn for his taking his parents to himself, his mother is never drawn, and Yusuf's words (99:8-14) have no speaker on stage and no plate. The cover is the bearer arriving (96:4)."
 },
